/target

# buck2's own build output tree (rustc invocations, linked artifacts,
# symlink farms, the local daemon's cached analysis, etc.) - entirely
# regenerated by `buck2 build`, just like /target/ was for cargo.
/buck-out/

# reindeer's cargo-registry-shaped scratch dir (a `[source.vendored-sources]
# directory = "vendor"` config.toml + registry cache) - only used while
# *running* `reindeer vendor`/`buckify` themselves (they shell out to cargo
# under the hood for dependency resolution), never read by buck2 at build
# time. Regenerated by `reindeer vendor`; unlike /third-party/vendor/ below,
# there's no reason to commit it.
/third-party/.cargo/

# /third-party/vendor/ (the actual vendored crate sources) and
# /third-party/BUCK (reindeer's generated rust_library targets) are
# INTENTIONALLY NOT ignored here - both are committed, same as reindeer's
# usual convention (see arelm): hermetic `buck2 build` for anyone who
# clones this repo, no reindeer/cargo/network access needed unless
# Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock actually changes.
